  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This guide is for the version of the Fire Genasi published in Monsters of the\n\tMultiverse. For the classic version of the Genasi, see our\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Genasi Handbook",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/races/genasi/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Fire Genasi is a descendent of efreeti, genies native to the elemental\n\tplane of fire. Prior to their update in Monsters of the Multiverse, the Fire\n\tGenasi was the only example of Constitution-based spellcasting and the only\n\texample of a variation of how Darkvision works (they saw in red instead of\n\tgray). While these mechanical hallmarks were lost, the other changes were\n\t(technically) additive."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While they have damage resistance and Darkvision, the Fire Genasi’s most\n\tsignificant trait is their innate spellcasting. The Fire Genasi get Produce\n\tFlame and Burning Hands, offering two decent low-level damage options. But\n\tthey are severely hampered by how exceptionally bad Flame Blade is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Flame Blade is basically unusable, serving essentially the same purpose as a\n\tcantrip at the cost of both Concentration and a leveled spell slot. Because\n\tit’s so bad, the Fire Genasi’s worthwhile traits can be easily replaced by a\n\tsingle level of sorcerer or wizard. Beyond that, the Fire Genasi is mostly\n\tjust a worse tiefling."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you’re dead set on playing a fire genasi, ask your DM if they’ll let you\n\tuse Aganazar’s Scorcher or Scorching Rays in place of Flame Blade. I can’t\n\tassume that they will, but I’ll hope that it works out for you."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
